{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25088 - PROTEIN:4736",
  "verbalization": "Galbanic Acid is shown to have a target relationship with HCT-8, a cell line that is also a target of multiple structurally diverse compounds, including (1R,3S,4R,6S)-3-[(R)-bromo-[(2R,3R,5S,6R)-3,5-dibromo-6-ethyloxan-2-yl]methyl]-6-ethynyl-2,5-dioxabicyclo[2.2.1]heptane and (2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[...]-oxane-3,4,5-triol. These compounds are all implicated in targeting the Phosphorylase b kinase gamma catalytic chain, skeletal muscle/heart isoform, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the regulation of this kinase. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, with varying scores indicating a strong association. The shared target suggests that Galbanic Acid may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of this kinase, which is involved in cellular processes such as glycogen metabolism and muscle function. The evidence supports a relationship between Galbanic Acid and the target kinase, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the role of the various compounds in this process.",
